# Website and Ordering

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M3 Story/sticker implementation locally reviewed; business facts/acceptance pending
Dependencies: 01_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo, 02_REFERENCES_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY.todo, 04_VISUAL_DESIGN.todo

## Purpose

Deliver a lightweight, editable site with clear direct-contact enquiries.

## Tasks

- [x] Begin only after the user authorizes implementation.
- [x] Establish a dedicated public site directory; never deploy the repository root.
- [x] Centralize business configuration and structured gallery data with stable IDs.
- [x] Build design tokens, responsive navigation, semantic sections and local/fallback fonts.
- [x] Build the real-photo hero, introduction and curated past-bake gallery.
- [x] Omit unconfirmed sizes, prices and availability instead of inventing them.
- [x] Implement product-specific, URL-encoded WhatsApp enquiries behind one configuration field.
- [ ] Activate WhatsApp after the actual public number is supplied.
- [x] Implement Instagram contact and optional configured public email/location.
- [x] Make the primary Instagram action a giant camera-logo button with a visible
  action label, accessible name and unchanged cream/green colours.
- [x] Make clear that clicking a message link does not send or confirm an order.
- [x] Keep the approved order home -> story -> cakes -> order with the original
  story/note and concise cake/order guidance; no FAQ, form or extra custom section.
- [x] Render transparent sticker variants while retaining full prepared JPG viewer links.
- [x] Complete current regression/public-boundary review through workstream 09.
- [ ] Add contact/service-area information and essential lead-time/allergen/payment rules.
- [x] Keep a contextual mobile enquiry CTA accessible without covering content or focus.
- [x] Use a small local gallery rather than a heavy live Instagram widget.
- [x] Include only prepared image derivatives with responsive sizing and loading behavior.
- [x] Keep core content and contact links usable without JavaScript.
- [x] Remove the message helper and make every cake enquiry a direct contact link.
- [x] Include the cake name in configured WhatsApp links; do not imply Instagram
  can receive a prefilled name or message.
- [x] Defer additional pages until genuine content justifies them.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] No shopping cart, login, payment collection or backend is invented for the MVP.
- [x] Enquiry preparation does not pretend to be checkout or automatic message delivery.
- [x] Gallery/contact data is updateable through central JSON files and a rebuild.
- [x] Real photos remain faithful to the supplied work.
- [ ] Final business facts and user acceptance are recorded before public release.

## Completion evidence

- npm run build produced 66 allowlisted public files in site/, including 20
  sticker variants. Current Node suite has 25 passing cases; workstream 09
  retains the five-case sticker/source checks.
- Node tests cover contact formatting/configuration, static output, media and
  publication boundaries. Browser evidence is in ..\.local\website-review\.
- Five cake cards and the order section link directly to the configured channel.
  The original story is the only restored section; no form, clipboard step, FAQ
  or separate custom-cake section remains.
- Source/server guidance: ..\docs\prototype-guide.md.

